{
  "id": "aristotles-illusion",
  "term": "Aristotle’s illusion",
  "definition": "Aristotle’s illusion is a tactile illusion in which a single object touched between crossed fingers is felt as if there were two objects. It is used to describe an alteration in how touch from adjacent fingers is perceived.",
